PART 7 — FUTURE ROADMAP (5–8 minutes)

What to say



"What you've seen today is the foundation. Here's where we're taking it next — focused on two themes: deeper account-level drill-down, and expanded pipeline hygiene scenarios."



A. Account-Level Drill-Down (Future)

What exists today





Bridge bar → account cards (all fields visible, SharePoint link)



Bridge search → find any account and see bridge placement



Dashboard HD → AD → AM → pipeline grid



Governance HD → AD → AM → deal grid

What we're building next

1. Customer 360° view
Click any customer name → see all bids for that customer across statuses, products, and quarters in one panel. Today we show one bid per card; the 360° view aggregates the full relationship.

2. Account timeline
Per customer: chronological view of every Opp Status change, activation date change, and modification — merged from version history across all their bids. Answers: "What's the full story on this account this quarter?"

3. Account-level bridge contribution
Show how much each customer contributes across multiple bars — e.g. same customer in Won + Top 5 in-flight + Churn. Today each bid appears once; the 360° view shows total account impact on Net Forecast.

4. Click-through from Governance → Bridge
From a stale deal in Governance, jump directly to where that deal sits on the Performance Bridge (or why it's excluded). Closes the loop between "this deal is stale" and "this deal is inflating the forecast."

5. Account comparison mode
Select 2–3 accounts and compare side-by-side: status, days stale, bridge value, activation date, ownership. Useful in deal review meetings.

6. Customer search as a first-class entry point
Global search: type customer name → get pipeline grid results + bridge placement + governance flags (stale? recent flip?) in one result card.



