What we're building next

1. Backward status flips (anomaly detection)
Flag deals that moved backward — e.g. Won → Proposed, Billed → Opportunity. These are data quality or process violations. Today we show all flips; next step is a dedicated anomaly filter.

2. Missing mandatory fields
Queue for in-flight deals missing critical fields: no Expected Activation, no Account Director, no GA Lines/MRC, no Customer Code. Prevents bad data from entering the bridge silently.

3. High-value stale deals
Combine stale queue with value threshold — e.g. "Proposed > 30 days and MRC > X." Prioritize cleanup by revenue impact, not just age.

4. Activation date integrity





Expected activation in the past but still Proposed/Opportunity (partially built — overdue activation)



Expected activation changed multiple times (version history on activation field)



Activation in Q3 but Opp Status still Lead/Opportunity

5. Billed without prerequisites
Deals marked Billed where Contract Signed date is empty, or Expected Activation is still in the future. Catches premature status updates.

6. Duplicate / overlapping bids
Same customer + same product + same quarter with multiple open bids. Surfaces double-counting risk in the bridge.

7. Ownership gaps
Deals with missing or changed AD/AM — especially after org changes. Track reassignment via version history on ownership fields.

8. Week-over-week pipeline movement
Compare pipeline snapshot this week vs last week: what's new, what's gone, what changed value. Shows pipeline velocity, not just point-in-time hygiene.

9. Hygiene scorecards by leader
Weekly HD/AD/AM scorecard: % of book stale, count of overdue activations, backward flips, missing fields. Drives accountability in QBRs.

10. Automated hygiene alerts (Cursor Automations / email)
Scheduled digest: "21+ day stale deals in your vertical" or "5 backward flips today" sent to HD/AD. Dashboard finds it; automation pushes it.



